    "type": "map",
    "unlocated": [
      {
        "backlog": "Retry Overpass once it is reachable again: a tag search (way[\"building\"] or way[\"man_made\"]) inside the 'PSI West' sub-area (near 47.5368N, 8.2222E, inside OSM way 28028409) should find the Ring Cyclotron building even without a name tag, the way DESY's unnamed halls were found by proximity to the HERA ring. Alternatively, request PSI's own site-plan/GIS layer.",
        "entity_id": "accelerator:psi-hipa",
        "entity_name": "High Intensity Proton Accelerator",
        "entity_type": "accelerator",
        "reason": "The HIPA Ring Cyclotron's own building has no distinctly-named OpenStreetMap element: Nominatim name searches for 'Ringzyklotron PSI', 'Ring Cyclotron PSI Villigen', 'Zyklotron' and 'Cyclotron' (bounded to the PSI campus) all returned zero results, and the tag/bbox-based Overpass search that would find an unnamed building near the accelerator could not run -- both overpass-api.de and lz4.overpass-api.de refused every connection attempt for the entire PSI/KIT portion of this session. site:psi-villigen's own coordinate (precision_m 800) is too coarse to derive a 48 m-circumference ring's position from.",
